                <pb facs="0298" n="198" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg198"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/24834</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-12-30"><hi rendition="#italic">December 30,
                        1920</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received January 11, 1921.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 3552</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Associated Press
                    despatch from Paris, published in the local press on December 22nd, in regard to
                    a statement purported to have been made by the French Minister for Foreign <pb
                        facs="0299" n="199" xml:id="pg199"/> Affairs to the effect that France will
                    not accord recognition to Mexico until the United States is prepared to do so,
                    (see pages 4 and 5, Embassy’s despatch No. 3542, of December 24, 1920<anchor
                        n="35" xml:id="d255-f1"/>), I have the honor to report that <hi
                        rendition="#italic">El Universal</hi> in its issue of the 29th reported that
                    Mr. Victor Ayguesparsse, the French Chargé d’Affaires here, had received a cable
                    from the French Ministry for Foreign Affairs, denying categorically the above
                    mentioned statement, and adding that the French Foreign Office has made no
                    declaration whatsoever about Mexico.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">George T.
                    Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
